/*
 * MotoGuard - NEO-6M -> ESP32 -> Firebase Realtime Database
 * Library: Firebase_ESP_Client (Mobizt) + TinyGPSPlus
 *
 * - GPS is read continuously in loop() (core 1); it is never blocked by network code.
 * - A separate FreeRTOS task (core 0) uploads to Firebase once per second.
 * - Only a VALIDATED fix is reported as GPS_ONLINE. Otherwise gpsFix=false / GPS_LOST.
 * - No fake coordinates are ever generated.
 *
 * ADDED: PASSKEY layer (HMAC-SHA256)
 * - The passkey is NEVER sent over WiFi/Firebase. Only HMAC proofs are exchanged.
 * - Pairing: ESP32 publishes a random challenge, the app answers with
 *   HMAC(passkey, "APP|"+challenge). If it matches, the ESP32 is "paired"
 *   (remembered in flash, survives reboot) and starts uploading real GPS data.
 * - Every upload carries a "sig" = HMAC(passkey, canonical data) so the app can
 *   verify the data really comes from a device that knows the passkey.
 */

